# OpenZone Bridge -- configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in. `.env` is gitignored and MUST NEVER
# be committed: the bot token alone is full control of your Discord guild.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing in `.env` is ever logged, echoed, or sent to the game client. The
# DayZ server is the only party that talks to this bridge, and it authenticates
# with OZ_SHARED_SECRET below -- not with anything from Discord.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Discord bot
#
# ALL FOUR ARE OPTIONAL, TOGETHER (TZ-2 R2.6, "the bridge without a bot").
#
# Leave DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN empty and the bridge still starts and still serves
# everything that lives in its own database -- chat, news, factions, the wipe.
# What it loses is the guild: no mirrors, no slash commands, no /link, and
# every one of them says so instead of failing quietly. GET /v1/ping answers
# {"ok":true,"discord":false} in that mode and {"...":true} with a bot, so the
# game and the admin can tell "the bridge is down" from "the bridge is up and
# has no bot". Nobody is linked without a bot, so players are named by their
# in-game name (Steam64 when even that is unknown).
#
# With a token the other three become REQUIRED: half a Discord configuration
# is a mistake, an absent one is a mode, and the bridge refuses to start on
# the first rather than guessing.
#
# Discord Developer Portal -> your application -> Bot -> Reset Token.
# SECRET. Never paste this anywhere except this file.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# Developer Portal -> General Information -> Application ID.
# Not secret; it appears in every invite link.
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=

# Right-click your test server in Discord (with Developer Mode on) -> Copy Server ID.
# Not secret.
DISCORD_GUILD_ID=

# The TEXT channel private conversation threads are created under. Required
# whenever a token is set, because a private thread can only live under a text
# channel. Right-click the channel -> Copy Channel ID.
DISCORD_PARENT_CHANNEL_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The bridge
BRIDGE_PORT=8787

# Which interface the bridge listens on. The DayZ server is the only party
# that talks to it, so the default is loopback: a bridge on the same host as
# the game server needs nothing else. Set 0.0.0.0 only behind a TLS
# terminator, and read the Security section of README.md first.
# BRIDGE_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Shared secret between the DayZ server and this bridge.
#
# It travels in the REQUEST BODY, not a header: DayZ's RestContext.SetHeader
# controls only Content-Type, so there is no way to send Authorization. That is
# why a public deployment must be https -- over plain http this value is
# readable by anyone on the path.
#
# Generate a long random one, e.g.:  openssl rand -hex 32
# The same value goes into the game server's
# $profile:OpenZone\OZ_Core_Settings.json -> Bridge.Secret
OZ_SHARED_SECRET=

# How long the bridge holds a poll request open before answering "nothing yet".
#
# MUST stay under ten seconds. Measured against the engine: an asynchronous
# DayZ request dies at exactly 10 s whatever RestApi.SetOption is told, and the
# bridge's answer then arrives in a socket nobody is listening on -- which
# looks, from the game, like a bridge that never answers. The documented
# 3..120 s range holds for the synchronous call only.
POLL_HOLD_SECONDS=8

# Optional. The roles whose holders count as bridge admins (personas,
# /openzone, and the storage admin page when its sign-in is on) alongside
# anyone with the Discord Administrator permission. One or more role ids,
# comma-separated. Right-click the role (Developer Mode on) -> Copy Role ID.
DISCORD_ADMIN_ROLE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- state
# Where the bridge keeps everything it remembers: links, conversations, the
# chat tail, news. One SQLite file; the directory is created if missing.
# Not secret, but treat the file as a small database -- back it up.
# BRIDGE_DB=./state/bridge.sqlite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chat
# How long a map mark shared into a conversation lives before the bridge
# deletes it from the thread and from its own store. Seconds; default 300.
# MARK_TTL_SECONDS=300

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- storage boxes
# Only on a host that also runs the DayZ server with OpenZone_Storage: the
# server profile's OpenZone/Storage/xchg directory. Unset = storage routes
# refuse and the game shows its boxes as unavailable.
STORAGE_XCHG_DIR=
# Versions older than this go, except each box's current one.
STORAGE_KEEP_VERSIONS_DAYS=14
# Events older than this go.
STORAGE_KEEP_EVENTS_DAYS=90

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- research
# Only on a host that also runs the DayZ server with OpenZone_Research: the
# server profile's OpenZone directory (the one that holds the
# OZ_Research_*.json configs). The bridge reads the configs from there,
# keeps every version, and leaves candidate configs for the game under
# research/xchg. Unset = research routes refuse; the game keeps its configs
# to itself and the VPP editor still works.
RESEARCH_DIR=
# The exchange directory, when it is not research/xchg under RESEARCH_DIR.
# RESEARCH_XCHG_DIR=
# Versions older than this go, except each config's current one and any
# candidate the game has not answered.
RESEARCH_KEEP_VERSIONS_DAYS=30
# Journal entries and answered commands older than this go.
RESEARCH_KEEP_EVENTS_DAYS=90
# The game server's profiles/OpenZone directory on this machine (defaults
# to RESEARCH_DIR): the core writes classes.tsv there at every start -- the
# server's classes with parents and game names -- and the bridge reads it
# into the class index every editor of the admin site checks against.
# PROFILE_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- admin web
# The storage admin page (design 2026-09-19, sections 8 and 15): boxes, a
# box's grid and contents, history and the difference between versions, a
# player's takings, a class across the server, the shelf of parked roots,
# health; changes to a closed box. Its own listener, ALWAYS on 127.0.0.1.
# 0 turns it off.
ADMIN_PORT=8788

# Sign-in with Discord for that page turns on with ADMIN_URL below. OPTIONAL:
# leave ADMIN_URL empty and the page has no sign-in at all -- safe only
# because nothing but this machine reaches 127.0.0.1. Never put a reverse
# proxy in front of the page in that mode.
# Without ADMIN_URL the bridge refuses requests that a proxy forwards.
#
# With ADMIN_URL the page sends admins to Discord and admits holders of one
# of the roles in DISCORD_ADMIN_ROLE_ID. Then these are REQUIRED as well:
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET, DISCORD_CLIENT_ID, DISCORD_GUILD_ID and
# DISCORD_ADMIN_ROLE_ID. Half of it set, and the page stays down while the
# bridge names the key.
#
# The address of the admin page as a browser sees it: what your reverse
# proxy serves (https://admin.example.com/storage), or http://localhost:8788
# on the machine itself. The Developer Portal -> OAuth2 -> Redirects must list
# exactly  <ADMIN_URL>/auth/callback  -- Discord accepts http for localhost
# only, so a remote host means https behind your proxy.
ADMIN_URL=

# Developer Portal -> OAuth2 -> Client Secret (Reset Secret). SECRET. Read
# only when ADMIN_URL is set.
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The map page: the world's size in metres for the coordinate grid
# (Chernarus is 15360) and, optionally, a map image the bridge serves
# under the boxes' pins, stretched to that size.
# ADMIN_MAP_SIZE=15360
# ADMIN_MAP_IMAGE=
